Photo by @BrianSkerry
A lemon shark pup swims within the shallow water of a mangrove on the island of Bimini in The Bahamas. Mangroves are natural nurseries for juvenal marine animals and sharks like this pup spend the first 2-3 years of their lives living here, until they’re big enough to go out an compete on the reefs. Protection of mangroves ensures healthy oceans. Photographed on assignment for @natgeo.
@thephotosociety @natgeocreative #sharks #mangroves #nature #photooftheday #bahamas #babyanimals

Photo by @GerdLudwig. A scene at the edge of the Salton Sea suggests that the area has seen better days. To see a photo of the same spot shot 7 years prior, look at the image I posted on my Instagram feed a week ago. The fluctuation in sea level and increased salinity of the Salton Sea have led to an environmental decay that is now nearing catastrophic dimensions. I’ve photographed the Salton Sea repeatedly over the past years and witnessed many changes over time. 
To explore the Salton Sea area today, join me for my documentary photography workshop, “The Art of Storytelling - The Salton Sea.” There are only a few spots left, information & sign up here: http://www.gerdludwig.com/?p=4298 
